From 8e23fc52e94f44ae2860c13d78642314a8737b2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:58:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(front): follow a substituted constant in the
 subscript of [][Next]_v as TLC does

TLC gives a declared constant the configuration substitutes, `C <- D`,
the OpDefNode of D as its tool object (processConstants), so its
SubscriptCollector enters D's body as an operator, whatever TLC
computed of D as it started. The front end declined any subscript that
named such a constant. It now enters the body of a definition without
parameters that substitutes a declared constant, and declines only
where the substitute is something else: a definition the
configuration substitutes for, or a Java method's.
